Z||000000||Spektyr||04-27-2001||09:35 PM||||Not being as much of an 'Under the car' mechanic as a 'Under the hood' mechanic', I don't know as much about transmissions as I'd like to.<P>What I do know is that my 85GT V6 4speed will LEAP off the line in 1st and redline in about 1.5 seconds.  2nd gear will run to about 50mph tops and 3rd goes a lot faster than I need to go on the street.  4th gear does about 3k rpm at 70mph giving me a theoretical rpm limited top speed of 140mph (but I bet I'm drag limited a bit under that).<P>I love driving this car, but I'd like a bit longer in 1st, maybe 35mph at redline, and I'd like to be able to reach 60-65mph in 2nd, just so I can brag about my 0-60 times.  I'd also like to get the rpm under 3k at 70-75mph in top gear so I can get some better economy on the highway (not to mention a higher theoretical top end).<P>The motor I have planned for this car will be in the 250-300hp neighborhood, so I'm not too worried about a steeper 1st gear, but it would be nice if it still ran fast in my somewhat stock 2.8 that should be putting out about 150-160 hp in a few weeks.<P>What transmissions do I need to find to accomplish this goal?<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||5
Z||000001||pontiacs4me||04-27-2001||10:51 PM||||taller tires in the back.  thats what I did with mine, one because it fills the wheel gap better, and 2 because of the trip im taking in 10 days.  I run a couple hundred rpm less on the highway, and every mpg counts when you drive to california.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||04-28-2001||12:35 AM||||I don't know about the Isuzu, but with a Getrag, 245/60-15 rear tires, and a 6500 RPM redline you can clear 60 in 2nd.<BR>I'm also doing just about 90 at 3000 RPM.<BR>A Getrag ought to hold 250-300 Hp as long as it's not abused.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||04-28-2001||12:43 PM||||The Getrag's the way to go for you.<BR>As for the Getrag handling power, Archies<BR>got a Getrag behind Rich Warbers 450 HP V8<BR>with no problems what-so-ever.<BR>There's also Jacks LT-1 V8 with 450-475 HP<BR>with Getrag that is driven hard and still<BR>has no probs. tough enough i'd say. ;-)<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spektyr||04-28-2001||05:34 PM||||Okay, so how can I tell the Izusu and Getrag tranny's apart in the junkyard?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||04-28-2001||10:50 PM||||The yard man will want $$$$ for the Getrag and only $$ for the Isuzu.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spektyr||04-29-2001||12:24 AM||||Hehe, I'm sure he will, but I'd like to know if it's a Getrag before I start pulling it out of the car.<P>And you give the Kansas junk yards too much credit.  I'd lay good odds the hillbillies running the yards around here wouldn't know a Fiero part if I whacked them upside the head with it.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||04-29-2001||04:12 AM||||Getrag's came in late 86 thru 88 V-6 cars.<BR>Isuzu's came in 85 thru 88 4-cyl.<BR>Just make sure it's an original 5-spd out of a V-6 car.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Will||04-29-2001||09:47 AM||||Any five speed that was used with a V6 in any FWD GM product is a Getrag. The non-Fiero Getrags had a slightly different shifter mechanism. It doesn't work directly with Fiero brackets, but <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  sells brackets with which it will work.||||reg||1
